    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322-a2">

                <pb facs="0755" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg707"/>

                <head>Commander Carter to Mr.
                        Van Valkenburgh.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Steamer Monocacy</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Off Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 2, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information a copy of the arrangements made this day by the naval and military
                    commanders of the treaty powers for the protection and defense of the foreign
                    settlement of Yokohama.</p>
                <p>I shall be obliged if you will send me a copy of the second letter, written and
                    signed conjointly by the ministers, on the subject of restricting the Japanese
                    entering Yokohama to those provided with a pass from one of the consulates.</p>
                <p>Some of the commanders who were at the conference had been furnished with a copy
                    of the above letter, but I have not yet received one.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. P. CARTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Commander.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Vankenburgh</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States in
                            Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d322-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d322-a2-a1"/>
